WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.720
In the previous video, we started working on our ruin.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.720
We took off the roof, and had a better
look at the structure itself.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.525
It's rough and basic.

00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:11.467
Patched together brickwork with some additional things
stuffed in there with cement.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.599
It misses some essential structural strength on the bottom,
and the top wall is very weak.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.963
Taking it down is probably cheaper and easier.

00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:22.880
But, we like to try and keep as much as possible
of the materials in our existing state.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.280
So, first up is reinforcing.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.040
So, we have a strong base.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.080
So, yeah, welcome to new Project Kamp update!

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.337
Let's get started!

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.840
So, this is the bottom of the ruin, built out of granite.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.120
Which makes it very strong, and the floor is leaning on top.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.960
Except for this part right here.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.040
This is made from bricks.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.040
Which is not structurally strong enough to hold the entire floor...

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.520
So, we need to reinforce this part.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.934
We're going to probably make a metal frame,
to make sure not all the load is on the bricks.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.440
But, actually on a strong frame.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.680
And, the frame would be coming here, on the granite.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.640
So the first thing we're going to do is clean up this edge,
 so we can measure it, and make a proper frame.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.360
And, the floor down here, in this room,
 is also not leveled at all...

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.680
There, it's super low in that corner,
and there it's very high...

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.285
So, as we're working with the hammer
to clean up the edge...

00:01:10.285 --> 00:01:12.840
We're probably also just going to clean up this one.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.200
And, after that level it, to make sure we have a good base.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.200
So, time to hammer!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.280
All right, so, the stone work is now done.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.280
This edge here is leveled and straight.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.480
So, now, we're going to make a metal frame
that supports the roof!

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.800
After we have cut the frame into its size,
it's time to weld it together.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.920
We're using a 12 centimeter H-beam, to carry the load.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.600
It's the thickest, heaviest object
we've made here so far, from metal.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.880
So, taking it down is a bit of a challenge...

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.698
Let's see how that goes.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.040
After we managed to carry it down...

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.338
We gave it a paintjob, so it's ready to go in.

00:04:34.464 --> 00:04:36.326
And, moving it to here was already challenging...

00:04:36.326 --> 00:04:39.951
But, what's actually a way bigger challenge 
is getting it up that edge...

00:04:40.454 --> 00:04:42.240
Mainly because it's just heavy.

00:04:42.366 --> 00:04:45.865
But, what made it more challenging,
is that we can't just easily put it on there...

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.840
Since it's quite a tight space and gap,
between the edge and the ceiling.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:54.000
It's like a centimeter, but the whole
ceiling and walls and wobbling and curved...

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.080
So, we ask a few hands to help out,
 and try to bring the thing into its position.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:02.040
It worked fine in terms of lifting,
but unfortunately, it didn't fit.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.080
Still some wobbly wall.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.586
So yeah, we needed to bring it down again, 
cut it once more and then try it again...

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.040
And finally, with the help of all hands on Project Kamp, we made it!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.600
We managed to lift it again, and fit it perfectly.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.160
So, now, we can continue with the renovation.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.640
After the bottom was reinforced, it was time to have 
a look at this beautiful brick wall on top.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.800
Hey! Today, we're going to have a look
at this very beautiful wall.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.720
It's very sketchy wall, and it's not stable at all.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.040
And, we want to chop out piece here.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.400
The main reason is because
the wall is already very terrible here.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.080
So, we have to rebuild it anyway.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:20.560
And, we're going to make space, to insert a sliding door frame,
with a frame from Rita's mom!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.560
So, this would also become
the main entrance of the building.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.920
But, we're a bit scared of that wall,
because it's very unstable at this point...

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.600
So, then, I made a very good safety measurement.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:36.000
It's this sketchy wall, connected to this sketchy wall,
which makes sure they don't fall over.

00:06:40.681 --> 00:06:41.800
Don't tighten it too much!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.119
You pull the wall in!

00:06:44.119 --> 00:06:47.000
We put a little bit of hardly any tension in it.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.497
And yet, the whole wall is shaking.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.440
So the first thing we got to do is cut a line,
 and then brick by brick, we're going to take it down.

00:06:55.566 --> 00:06:58.926
Ideally, we save as much as possible,
so we can rebuild some holes.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:03.040
Tim is getting ready there in the shade.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.080
- I think it's safe, Tim.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.080
- I think it's safe as we can make it!

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:44.000
All right, so, the wall is now out,
and it went surprisingly easy!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.000
I think we almost save all the bricks,
because they were not really stuck.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.309
And, now, at the end of the day, 
we're going to cement it a bit back.

00:08:53.309 --> 00:08:55.960
The holes in the frame, with the lintel here on top.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.840
But, now, it's going to be too warm...

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:00.840
So, we're going to take a little siesta, and continue.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.412
See you later.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:04.821
Straight line.

00:09:05.324 --> 00:09:06.539
Not a straight line...

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.240
Special announcement!

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.972
All right, so we are looking for a new video maker!

00:09:21.224 --> 00:09:25.520
So, at the beginning of the season, 
we had Felix helping us out to make videos for Season 2.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.880
But unfortunately, he has to stop for a few reasons.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.960
Because, it's just heavy on the setting to edit videos.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.334
Flies, it's hot, not a stable office...

00:09:36.334 --> 00:09:39.299
But, also, really producing a video each week is quite intense...

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.520
He's not used to that.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:45.600
And, in general, I think also just YouTube comments,
and a lot of opinions can make it hard.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.000
So, unfortunately, he won't be able to continue.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.800
So, we're looking for a new video maker.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:54.080
We're actually aiming to get to two,
 to also just reduce the workload on the video maker itself.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.120
So, this is a request to you guys.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.720
If you're interested in making videos here, come and help out.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.720
Or, maybe your friends that want to come.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:06.528
And, we wrote an article or a community post on YouTube.

00:10:06.528 --> 00:10:09.164
Includes more information, with also the reasons why Felix stopped.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.249
Also, with what we're looking for!

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:16.920
In short, making videos until the end of the season,
which would be November.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:21.720
And then, until Update 70, so,
 you can do the math until when that is.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.520
It will be producing a weekly video.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:30.840
So, if you're interested, make sure to read that post,
with all the information and a sign-up to help out.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.221
Now: back to the ruin!

00:11:20.352 --> 00:11:22.640
So, it's now end of the day, and we're in the shade.

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:26.705
We started cleaning the bricks, to get the old cement off.

00:11:26.705 --> 00:11:30.320
They're now here, and Tim it's putting them back together.

00:11:32.134 --> 00:11:33.600
So, the frame sticks in there.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.062
So, we built this up with the lintel on top, 
and then, it should be good.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.200
Next, we're going to add the windows.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.480
We will add some in the bottom.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.999
So, it's not a dark cave...

00:12:36.999 --> 00:12:41.160
And, in the top, to fill the window holes,
 that are already there.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.600
And, we got in touch with Ronald.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.560
He had a bunch of glass, and window frames left-over, 
from his home renovation, a few years ago.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.667
He gave it to us for our future buildings.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:54.400
For the ruin, we are going to use the double glass,
 and he has a few cool wooden frames for that!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.960
So, here we have some windows!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:02.120
We have this one, which is a window 
with double glass, which is cool!

00:13:03.327 --> 00:13:05.840
With the frame, but not the external frame...

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.120
So, we would need to make that...

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.240
A big door.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:16.240
And, there is also a whole stack of this double glass!

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.800
I think he ordered it, but it was wrong
or something for his house?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:24.120
So, it's pretty new,
but it doesn't have any framing around it.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:27.000
We need to find a way to add those.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:31.131
I think we're going to use this one, 
and this one for the ruin.

00:13:32.972 --> 00:13:35.120
Our wood tools are not very advanced yet...

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.160
So, we brought it to a local wood guy, 
to make a frame around it.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:44.400
And, he made the frames pretty basic:
 not angled, and no water drainage in there.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.400
We would think the water would just flow inside...

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.880
But, his suggestion was to put the frames under a small angle.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:54.120
So, the entire frame, and the water then just flows out.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:57.480
Which, is apparently a very common to do around here.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:01.080
Bit skeptical about his approach,
but hey, it's a sketchy ruin.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:01.760
So, let's see!

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.920
So, here we have windows that all are already there.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:11.080
And, our windows that we just made are somewhat fitting...

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:15.720
The height fits in, but they need to have
a few centimeters chopped out...

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:19.280
We're probably going to chop a bit,
 on the left and the right.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:22.120
So, that we can keep the lintel above.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:25.120
And then, the windows should fit in!

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:05.764
So, before, we were working a lot with the stairs.

00:15:05.764 --> 00:15:07.920
Just because that was the only thing we had...

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:11.400
But now, we asked George, our neighbour,
if he has some scaffolding.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.880
So, he borrowed us some very classic, 
traditional, Portuguese scaffolding!

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:24.960
A bit rusty, bit heavy, 
but this is the thing they use around here!

00:15:25.237 --> 00:15:27.035
So yeah, we're going to put it up,

00:15:27.035 --> 00:15:31.168
And, from then on, we should be able to work better at a height,

00:15:31.168 --> 00:15:35.475
Especially, if we start doing the windows upstairs, and the roof.

00:15:35.475 --> 00:15:36.720
Let's puzzle this together!

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:40.417
Safety switches...

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:41.760
Stairs...

00:15:42.666 --> 00:15:43.861
Stackable!

00:15:44.716 --> 00:15:46.709
A cross that goes in the back...

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.080
And, the wooden shelf!

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:17.422
Very safe!

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.760
So, next, we're going to do the two windows here on top.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:25.960
They're going to be slightly different,
because we are first going to put it in a granite frame.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.840
And then, the wooden one, 
and it's a bit more of a proper way of doing it.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.800
It's also very common, actually, to do around here.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.680
Because, you find a lot of granite,
 and many of the houses here have that frame.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:40.360
So, we've got some granite,
we got the wooden frames, some cement...

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.800
Now, we're just going to build them in here!

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.800
All right, so, let me show you the final result!

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:11.312
So, we now have a window that can open,
which creates a good airflow with the door.

00:18:12.117 --> 00:18:15.651
Another window here, that gives a good view to the outside.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:19.275
A reinforced frame, to make sure the whole thing doesn't collapse.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:25.560
Then on the outside, we have the big hole,
 for the big sliding door.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:29.640
It's not installed yet, because you first
want to do a bit more work on the inside...

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:33.240
And, you might think:
''How do you get into that door?''

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:37.800
So, the plan is to build a bit of a balcony
here in front, so that you can sit outside.

00:18:38.311 --> 00:18:40.711
And, this would also be the main entrance.

00:18:41.113 --> 00:18:45.000
The main reason also for doing that,
is that this door is just really low...

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:51.480
So, we're going to close this one up,
and then we can also arrange the interior a bit easier.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.840
Over here, we have a window frame from the granite.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:57.571
All finished, and ready to put in the wood!

00:18:58.024 --> 00:19:02.776
It's under a slight angle to make sure the water,
and the rain flows out, and not in...

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:06.460
We already put in a frame,
just so you can see what it looks like.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.847
Yeah, it's very convenient if I look outside,
 I look straight at the granite...

00:19:11.847 --> 00:19:14.702
A nd, to really see the view,
I just do a bit of bending.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:19.040
And, next, we also actually wanted to take out this wall!

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.840
Because, you have an awesome view back here.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.400
But, we're a bit scared of taking out this one at this point...

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:28.346
Because, it gives strength to that wall,
which is still very fragile.

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:32.520
So, the next step would actually be to build a wooden frame.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.120
And, that makes everything structurally strong, 
and connected together.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.240
We're also going to look into the insulation, 
on what to do with that...

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:44.600
If you're already on to see the next video, 
make sure to subscribe on Patreon, so you can see it!

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.880
Or not, and just continue to watch here.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.880
See you next Monday, with the new video!

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:51.120
That was it for this one!

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.880
Thanks for watching, and see you next time!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.231
Wanna look at the view?

